{"format":1,"key":"zone:winterspring","path":"/lore/zone/winterspring","name":"Winterspring","kind":"zone","label":"Zone","zone":{"key":"winterspring","name":"Winterspring","path":"/lore/zone/winterspring"},"levels":"","description":"Winterspring is a vast, snow-covered valley nestled high along the northeastern slopes of Mount Hyjal, directly above the enchanted forests of Moonglade…","intro":[],"clips":[{"id":"zone:winterspring","part":"narration","anchor":"story","title":"The story","paras":["Winterspring is a vast, snow-covered valley nestled high along the northeastern slopes of Mount Hyjal, directly above the enchanted forests of Moonglade and Felwood. Known for its bitter cold, ancient Highborne ruins, and wandering apex predators, the region is anchored by the neutral goblin outpost of Everlook. It remains a land of fierce natural perils, sheltering remnants of the blue dragonflight while confronting demonic corruption along its southern heights.","Perched thousands of feet above the surrounding wilderness, Winterspring rests beneath crisp mountain air and relentless snowstorms. Enormous exposed roots of the World Tree, Nordrassil, cut through the snowdrifts like towering wooden arches, warped and twisted during the climactic struggles of the Third War. While much of northern Kalimdor is dominated by dense woodlands and warm climates, Winterspring is a quiet land of medium alpine forests, rocky bluffs, and frozen lakes, home to formidable frostsabers, chimaeras, yetis, and thick-furred winter bears.","Reaching this high plateau requires traversing the ancient carved passages of Timbermaw Hold, guarded by uncorrupted furbolgs who closely scrutinize any travelers passing from Felwood or Moonglade. At the valley's center sits Everlook, a thriving trading town operated by the Steamwheedle Cartel. Goblins welcome both Alliance and Horde adventurers with open registers, acting as an indispensable haven of engineering, trade, and warm fires against the biting mountain frost.","Centuries before modern settlements arose, ancient elves built the lakeside city of Kel'Theril. After reckless Highborne sorcerers shattered the cursed Crystal of Zin-Malor, madness claimed them, leaving restless phantoms to wander the ruined pillars and frozen waters to this day. Further south rise the cavernous heights of Mazthoril, the traditional Kalimdor stronghold of the blue dragonflight. Here, the brood of the Spell-Weaver Malygos, overseen by the matron protector Haleh, watches over arcane currents and contests local threats.","The serenity of Winterspring is sharply broken along its southernmost border at Darkwhisper Gorge. There, elite demonic forces, remnant legions from the Third War, crawl along jagged canyons blocking the high approaches toward the summit of Mount Hyjal. Meanwhile, the native Winterfall furbolgs have succumbed to foul corruptions, prompting independent researchers like Donova Snowden to investigate the encroaching taint before the entire valley's wildlife is consumed."],"hash":"c8197b","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"7e2ddee315","sec":147},"female-narrator":{"sha":"0d04062f1a","sec":157}}}],"sources":[{"kind":"wiki","title":"Winterspring (Classic)","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Winterspring_(Classic)"},{"kind":"wiki","title":"Winterspring","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Winterspring"}],"related":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/everlook","n":"Everlook","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/timbermaw-hold","n":"Timbermaw Hold","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/mazthoril","n":"Mazthoril","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/darkwhisper-gorge","n":"Darkwhisper Gorge","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/ruins-of-kel-theril","n":"Ruins of Kel'Theril","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/frostsaber-rock","n":"Frostsaber Rock","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/npc/donova-snowden","n":"Donova Snowden","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/npc/rivern-frostwind","n":"Rivern Frostwind","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/quest/3512-in-eranikus-own-words","n":"In Eranikus